course: dictionary
lesson: 2979
title: Doubtful looks
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Dubiously is an adverb, so it tells you how someone does something. It describes the way a person looks, speaks or acts when they are not sure, or do not trust what they see or hear. It comes from the same family as doubt, so if you spot doubt nearby, you are close to the meaning.
explain: Read the clues around the word. «The Rat looked dubiously at Toad's latest plan.» Rat is not sure the plan is safe or sensible. Ask: what word would fit here? Try doubtfully in the sentence instead. It still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
explain: Sometimes the words around it are the clue. In the story, the Rat says, «Very good news indeed, if only—if only——». The dashes show him trailing off, so he is speaking dubiously: he does not quite believe the good news will come true.
fact: Dubiously is an adverb, so it tells you how something is done.
fact: «Dubiously» means in a doubtful way: you are not sure something is true, good or safe.
fact: «Dubiously» can also mean in a way that is not quite honest, or in a way that people suspect.
fact: Dubiously often goes with «look», «say», «eye» and «sniff»: someone looks at a plan they do not trust.
fact: Doubtfully is a close synonym, so it is a good swap to check your meaning in a sentence.
exercise: «The Rat looked dubiously at Toad's latest plan.» What does dubiously tell you about how the Rat looked? | Happily, as if he loved the plan | *Doubtfully, as if he did not trust the plan | Quickly, as if he was in a hurry | Angrily, as if he wanted to fight
exercise: Toad says he will fly the boat over the river. Rat sniffs dubiously. What does this show? | Rat is delighted and wants to join in | *Rat is not sure the plan is safe | Rat is fast asleep | Rat is very hungry
exercise: What is a good swap for dubiously in «He eyed the soup dubiously»? | *Doubtfully | Happily | Quickly | Loudly
test: «Very good news indeed, if only—if only——», said the Rat dubiously. Why is the Rat speaking dubiously? | He is too tired to speak | *He is not sure the good news will really happen | He is cross with Toad | He is sure and very excited
test: Which sentence uses dubiously correctly to show doubt about safety? | He laughed dubiously at the joke. | He ate his lunch dubiously and quickly. | He sang dubiously in the bath. | *He stepped dubiously onto the rickety bridge.
exam: Which word is closest in meaning to dubiously? | Quickly | Happily | *Doubtfully | Loudly
